        "reasoning_content": "Let me carefully think through this task.\n\nThe user wants a single, self-contained HTML document that explains how AIVA/Grace works via a friendly cartoon visualization. Key requirements:\n\n1. **No external assets** — all SVG/CSS/Canvas inline, no fetches, no network.\n2. **Responsive styling**, legible labels, accessible buttons, reduced-motion support.\n3. **Polished explainer, not a wall of text.**\n4. **Interaction contract**: `window.AIVA_DEMO` with `reset()`, `next()`, `togglePlay()`, `getState()`. `getState()` returns `{step: integer, playing: boolean}`. Exactly 7 steps (0–6). `reset()` sets step=0, playing=false, cancels playback. `next()` advances by one, clamped at 6. `togglePlay()` starts/stops auto-advance, stops at step 6. Starts at step 0, paused. A visible element with `id=\"step-label\"` contains the current step's label. Visible buttons with ids \"next\", \"reset\", \"play\" invoke the matching API methods. Real DOM buttons, visible/usable on desktop and mobile.\n5. **Sample request**: \"How does AIVA remember our conversation?\" flows through the system.\n6. **Steps** 0–6 as specified.\n7. **Cartoon characters** (drawn myself in inline SVG), moving message envelopes/tokens, clear arrows, active-stage highlight.\n8. **Optional-capabilities area** for Canvas/Imaging/MOSS, clearly outside the main chat path.\n9. **Animation readable**, all controls working.\n\nArchitecture facts to respect:\n- AIVA = PC-side companion runtime; Grace = conversational persona.\n- launch.sh orchestrates services.\n- AIVA Console = browser UI + standalone HTTP/WebSocket server.\n- User sends message via Console's `/api/telepathic/send`.\n- Console applies reversible Cypher encoding (not encryption).\n- Publishes to `/telepathic/stimulus` via rosbridge and ROS 2.\n- `telepathy_receptor` ROS node decodes and calls the Interactive Python library.\n- Interactive assembles Grace's persona, current time, user profile, recent conversation history.\n- Memory is an in-process Python library using SQLite, not a separate ROS node; by default up to 8 recent exchanges included; older exchanges are"
